+// Spawn de-collision (see syncWorld): how close two centres have to be to
+// count as the same point, how far along the view axis to step out of it, and
+// how many steps before giving up. The step clears the epsilon several times
+// over, so one step always escapes an occupied point, and 0.08 units is four
+// orders of magnitude above the depth resolution this projection has at
+// reading distance (~3e-5 units at z=5 with near 0.05 / far 200) -- the two
+// planes separate cleanly instead of z-fighting. The limit only has to cover
+// a plausible window count; past it a shared point is better than a quad
+// pushed into the near plane.
+static constexpr float kSpawnEpsilon   = 0.02f;
+static constexpr float kSpawnStep      = 0.08f;
+static constexpr int   kSpawnStepLimit = 48;
+
 // A normal damage cycle stops when nothing else in Hyprland changes. 3D mode is
 // itself an animated scene, so keep a small render pump alive while it is open.
